From 533e9f180ab7473d59e5a4e91cb2da90231a20fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:32:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 266/283] feat(execution): register environment variables and
 migration warnings

U4 environment-variable registry slice (on top of the U3 round-2 fix):

* add pypto.execution.env_registry as the single source of truth for the
  35 frozen migration variables plus 2 U4-discovered extras, 2 runtime
  thread variables and the registry warning switch (40 rows total);
  every row carries name/category/meaning/default/legal_domain/
  affects_artifact_semantics/replacement/deprecation status, consumer
  kind, semantic scope, digest verdict and static effect evidence;
* doctor reports the registry rows (allowlist, statuses, unregistered
  noise) and never emits raw values; sensitive unregistered names are
  redacted, host paths stay basename-only by default;
* compat layer: legacy names keep working, one-time deprecation warnings
  with declarative replacements, silence via
  PYPTO_X_ENV_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS=0, unregistered PYPTO_X_* reads warn
  once and show up in doctor;
* focused tests: 16 registry tests (frozen 35 completeness, one-time
  warnings, unregistered protection, digest invariance, doctor wiring,
  Python 3.7 AST); discovery tests updated for registry-driven rows and
  round-2 strictness.

No numeric behavior change; execution plan/report bytes unchanged for all
35 migration variables.  Perf: UNGATED.
